# AGENTS.md — `data/`

Root [`../AGENTS.md`](../AGENTS.md) applies without exception. Placement and
storage come from the marked contract in [`../README.md`](../README.md).

## Additional constraints

- `raw/` is immutable. Never modify, delete, rename, reformat, deduplicate, or
  “repair” an acquired payload. Express corrections and exclusions downstream.
- `interim/` and `processed/` are pipeline-owned. Do not create or edit their
  payloads by hand; fix and rerun the producing stage.
- Never stage payload bytes in Git. Real raw inputs use {{ data_versioning }};
  reusable processed data may be {{ data_versioning }}-snapshotted only after
  the user approves retaining or sharing that exact version.
- Do not treat a test fixture as acquired data or copy it into `data/raw/`.
- A real raw file needs a validated `metadata/` manifest entry. Adding/moving
  raw payloads, changing factual manifest mappings, and `{{ data_versioning }}
  push` are durable provenance actions requiring explicit user approval.

## Safe actions

You may fetch declared data with `{{ data_versioning }} pull`, read payloads,
run the pipeline, validate manifests, and inspect generated interim/processed
outputs. A surprising value is a reason to fail and investigate, never to patch
the bytes silently.
